In article <C617H1.M07@odin.corp.sgi.com> marci@relay.sgi.com (Marc Ishii) writes:

      Here you are, humming along the mines, toasting everything in your path
   with your newly aquired Gauntlets of power and +3 Demonbane (taken from
   that dead Dwarf Lord).  You get hungry, and spy a tasty egg on the ground.
   After a quick snack, you suddenly turn to stone after eating a cockatrice
   egg.  *sigh*

This brings up a question.  I had the same thing happen to me with one of
my best characters in a while.  Pretty stupid death, but the problem was
that my god was nice and happy, so I started praying as soon as I realized
that I was turning to stone.  Well I turned to stone in mid-prayer.  So
what's the use of having prayer help keep you from being stoned (as at
least the 3.0 source code shows), when it takes longer to too long to pray
for it to do any good?
	Also, how long does it take to eat a lizard corpse?  Same problem
there?


